    "trigger": "Valid Delivery order total10000 piastres, Multi splits Cash5000 + InstaPay5000 Pending, AmountPaid10000 (required plan tender parameter), valid delivery customer/service/address, authorized POS and dispatch actors, active driver, no refund. The immediate5000 cash leg posts at checkout. Ready and Assign are then invoked normally via existing API.",
    "evidence": [
      "CheckoutRules.SelectElectronicLeg50-63 creates pending electronic5000, ComputeIsPaid77-78 false; positive Multi DefersAllMoneyfalse. Handler255-265 posts non-electronicCash5000 and skips InstaPay; no Delivery+Multi restriction in checkout. Delivery row created223-229.",
      "DeliveryFactsComposer14-29 AmountToCollect=order.Total-refund=10000, PaymentAlreadySettled=order.IsPaid=false, PaymentMethod=Multi. It does not subtract already posted split cash5000.",
      "DeliveryRules11-12 for any non-Cash method with settledfalse returns WHOLE amount10000; CreateCashCustody18-20 sets Expected10000. MarkReady26-58 and Assign36-137 have no pending-electronic prohibition; actual Assign creates custody from facts87 and storesExpected100-105.",
      "RecordDeliveryResult expected94; absent CollectedAmount defaults expected95, sets delivery/custody collected10000 at99/108 and no reason because equal. If driver correctly reports remaining5000 with reason, custodyExpected10000 creates artificial5000 difference.",
      "Settlement scopes Collected amount as expected92 and can post actual10000 into Main110-117 in addition to earlierCash5000 if user really collects/remits full amount demanded by custody; no order paid/electronic transition or reversal of immediate leg in either Result or Settlement. If expected isdefault10000 but actual5000, stricter variance approval triggers even though immediate5000 already in till."
    ],
    "root_cause": "Delivery responsibility collapses per-leg payment collection into one whole-order IsPaid flag and Total-refund. Mixed pending order is partially collected, but modeled as wholly uncollected for driver custody.",
    "impact": "Overstated driver collection/custody by already posted immediate leg; possible duplicate customer collection or artificial driver variance/approval requirement. No claim actual customer payment, cash theft, SQL acceptance or persisted double revenue was reproduced.",
    "counterevidence": [
      "Requires a delivery Multi order with a pending electronic leg; all-immediate Multi IsPaidtrue yields zero driver responsibility, normal Cash COD has no immediate checkout treasury collection.",
      "Cash tender AmountPaid10000 is request-plan sufficient-payment field, not proof whole10000 actually received: handler only posts splitCash5000.",
      "FIN001 already blocks electronic confirmation, but does not block delivery Ready/Assign or eliminate immediate collection; this is distinct driver responsibility consequence, not second confirmation finding.",
      "A real cashier may choose not to dispatch unpaid electronic orders through UI, but server API does not enforce that guard.",
      "Settlement source/driver row locks are strong and prevent ordinary duplicate same-driver settlement; this candidate concerns wrong admitted monetary basis, not missing those locks."
    ],
    "correction_design": "Compute outstanding collectible amount from per-leg posted/confirmed state, including refund allocation, or explicitly reject unsupported mixed pending dispatch until valid payment resolution. Keep zero/prepaid/COD behavior and ensure result/settlement do not invent collection or duplicate earlier money.",
    "regression_tests": [
      "Valid deliveryCash5000+PendingElectronic5000 expected driver obligation must never include already postedCash5000; explicitly decide collectresidual vs dispatchblock.",
      "All-immediateMulti and pureCOD controls, partial refund allocation, confirmed/nonconfirmed electronic.",
      "Result default/explicit5000 and settlement actual5000 must not create false5000 variance.",
      "Existing FIN001 repair plus custody computation must avoid double confirm/cash fallback collection."
    ],
